# Environment configuration for the Trading Intelligence System.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env.
#
# Two provider integrations are implemented and active: FRED (macro
# data) and Alpha Vantage (technical price candles and news) — see
# README.md's Provider Abstraction section. Sentiment, and the Data
# Controller's own generic marketData domain, have no chosen provider
# yet; nothing is assumed or invented ahead of that.
#
# Three environments are recognized (see README.md's Environments
# section for detail):
#   development — local iteration; real FRED/Alpha Vantage calls only
#                 if the credentials below are set, otherwise
#                 synthetic/caller-supplied data
#   test        — `npm test`; synthetic/mocked in-memory fixtures
#                 only, never requires real credentials
#   production   — real provider adapters, real credentials
# No real credentials exist in this repo in any environment today —
# this file contains no real values.

# Port the (future) service listens on. Optional.
PORT=3000

# Environment name: development | test | production.
NODE_ENV=development

# --- Provider credentials -------------------------------------------
# FRED (Federal Reserve Economic Data) — macro data for the Macro
# Agent. Read ONLY in providers/fredMacroLiveSource.js.
FRED_API_KEY=

# Alpha Vantage — technical price candles (Technical Agent) and news
# (News Agent). Read ONLY in providers/alphaVantageMarketLiveSource.js
# and providers/alphaVantageNewsLiveSource.js.
ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=

# Sentiment, and the Data Controller's own generic marketData domain,
# have no chosen provider yet — no credential name exists for either
# because no adapter that would consume one has been built.
